{
  "id": "public-lp2-as-pad",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "LP2 as a running key for shorter Cicada texts",
  "question": "Does the unsolved LP2 rune stream, used as a skip-aware key, recover English from five specified Cicada objects?",
  "reader_question": "Could Liber Primus itself be the key to a shorter message?",
  "summary": "Replays the pinned F-01 inversion: five targets, four LP2 key forms, two signs, and a planted skip-aware control.",
  "finding": "No tested pairing passed the source's English score bar. The best of 40 decodes scored −7.032 against −5.500; the five highest scorers did not exceed their own shuffled-target maxima. A planted message was recovered exactly.",
  "limitations": "This is a cross-artifact key test, not a direct LP2 decrypt. The pp49–51 payload was unavailable, and all keys began at offset zero. The null was calculated only for the selected top five configurations; the hard-coded 63-byte AN END sequence is not independently authenticated here.",
  "next_steps": "A further LP2-as-key proposal should specify a verified target byte stream, its rune encoding, key offset, page boundary treatment and skip rule before searching.",
  "outcome": "not-supported",
